<title>GERMANY: Reuter poll on Bundesbank M3 money supply target.</title>
<headline>Reuter poll on Bundesbank M3 money supply target.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the tabulated results of a Reuter poll of economists on the likely decision of the Bundesbank council on its M3 money supply target, to be announced on Thursday.</p>
<p>Some economists believe that the central bank will switch to a two-year target from its usual one-year goal in the run-up to European monetary union.</p>
<p>They predicted that the growth corridor would be unchanged or slightly lower than the four to six percent rate set for 1996. M3 growth has overshot the target so far this year.</p>
